Ported from the TypeScript build's __tests__/cases/typescript/012-rust-block-comment-not-header.case.yaml; expected output is the TypeScript build's, except:
- A plain block comment at the top is the header comment when there is no `//!` comment; the TypeScript build read only `//` lines.
- Signatures print as written on one line (`fn main()`, not `fn main ()`), with generics, a const's or static's type, and a type alias's type; the TypeScript build printed keyword and name only, spaced out.
== args
input/block-comment.rs
== file input/block-comment.rs
/* This is a block comment */

fn main() {}
== stdout
input/block-comment.rs
This is a block comment
[L3-L3] fn main()
== stderr
== exit 0
